# Why this file exists — measured on this repo, not inherited.
#
# setuptools' legacy sdist default matches only `tests/test*.py`. It therefore
# omitted `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/__init__.py`. conftest.py defines the
# fixtures half the shipped suite depends on, so the suite that shipped inside
# the sdist could not run: installing the published 0.5.0 sdist and running its
# own tests/ gave **59 passed, 55 errors** — every error a fixture lookup
# failing at setup, across test_disparity, test_geographic, test_missing_column
# and test_report.
#
# This reproduces ONLY from a clean checkout. A local `python -m build` in a
# working tree that already has `hmda_analyzer.egg-info/` reuses the stale
# SOURCES.txt, which lists conftest.py, and produces a CORRECT sdist. Since
# `*.egg-info/` is gitignored, CI never has that seed — so the artifact CI ships
# is broken while the one a maintainer builds by hand looks fine. Verified: the
# file list of the 0.5.0 sdist on PyPI is identical to a fresh-clone build.
#
# SIXTH instance of this defect in the portfolio: sbic-tracker, oz-tracker,
# cdfi-fund-tracker and nmtc-mapper hit it first, then cdfi-benchmark as the
# fifth. This repo is the second of a four-repo sweep; cdfi-data and
# nmtc-application-builder follow as seven and eight. (Do not copy this ordinal
# forward unchanged -- four files all claiming to be the fifth is how the count
# stops being evidence.) The fix was written four times and propagated nowhere,
# so this change is paired with a `test-sdist` job
# in release.yml that unpacks the built tarball and runs ITS suite. The
# MANIFEST.in is only what makes that job pass; the job is what stops this from
# silently regressing. Packaging that is never installed from is packaging that
# is never verified.
recursive-include tests *.py

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include pyproject.toml

# pyproject.toml is load-bearing for the shipped suite beyond metadata: it
# carries [tool.pytest.ini_options], which registers the `live` marker. Without
# it in the tarball, a test-sdist run emits PytestUnknownMarkWarning and
# --strict-markers turns that into a collection error.

# The docs-check gate ships inside the sdist too, so the tarball carries
# everything needed to re-run the gate that certified it. Matches nmtc-mapper.
include docs-check.toml
include docs-check-denylist.txt
recursive-include tools *.py
recursive-include docs/README.expected *.txt

# examples/ is intentionally NOT shipped — the demo notebook is a repo artifact,
# not part of the distributed package.
prune examples

global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__/*
